{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>To give to them and to their seed after them.</b> Our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted: ״לתת להם״ — to give to them — these are the ones who came up from Egypt; ״ולזרעם״ — and to their seed — these are the ones who came up from Babylonia; ״אחריהם״ — after them — the days of the Messiah. Thus they interpreted in Devarim Rabbah. And it appears that they needed to interpret thus because we find three verses, each one adding progressively. That is, it is written (Deuteronomy 11:21): ״למען ירבו ימיכם וימי בניכם על האדמה אשר נשבע ה׳ לאבותיכם לתת להם כימי השמים על הארץ״, and at the end of והיה עקב (ibid.) it is written: ״לתת להם ולזרעם אחריהם ארץ זבת חלב ודבש״, and here it mentions ״לתת להם ולזרעם אחריהם״ — therefore they interpreted three inheritances."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:44:29.644712663Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}